The bodhisattva ideal: Śāntideva (@buddhist-bodhisattva: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhist-further-reading, #source @buddhist-source-bodhisattva, #philosophy @buddhist-middle-way, #buddhism @buddhist-middle-way) { r_7ZCDQRFNWQVDH1RBH833TZS72T
**Read:** Read the work in order, tracing bodhicitta, conduct, generosity, patience, and wisdom. Bodhicitta concerns the aspiration toward awakening for the benefit of beings; investigate how the text develops that aspiration rather than reducing it to a general wish to be helpful.

**Investigate:** Reconstruct an argument about anger, patience, or the concern for others. Compare its assumptions with an early teaching without treating different accounts of the goal as interchangeable. Return to the difficult wisdom chapter through the Madhyamaka reading.

**Check:** identify the passages, edition, and interpretation another reader would need to examine your account. Let the comparison modify an earlier view when the evidence warrants it.

**Source:** [The Way of the Bodhisattva — Bodhicaryāvatāra](../sources/Bodhisattva.lingua#r_1SRX10622ZA3EHMDH1PVQFC344).

